# stash_record_witness.rish -- a record parked in the dead-letter box and never read back out.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/stash_record_witness.rish
#
# REDS %464. `tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh` stashes a dead lap's unsent work at the round open --
# correct, and the only reason those bytes survive (%321). What was missing is the read back, so
# the bytes lived on while the record stayed lost: three stashes on this field held 32 files, 455
# insertions, and three complete session logs that stood in the box alone. One of them recorded a lap whose CODE had landed,
# so the work shipped and its reasoning did not, and the next lap paid to rediscover it.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, hard: `unlanded=0`. A session log inside a round-open stash stands in the
# worktree, or on a branch A READER WILL ACTUALLY REACH -- local or remote-tracking, outside the
# `pier/` namespace.
#
# THE PARK IS NOT A LANDING (REDS %507). The round open fills two drawers, and until `20260906`
# one certified the other empty: it stashes an unsent tree, and it parks a diverged line on
# `refs/heads/pier/diverged-<stamp>`. `%499` measured where those go -- 11 park branches on `xy`,
# 33 distinct subjects since `20260828`, ten of them standing there still. So the elder reading,
# which walked `refs/heads` and `refs/remotes` whole, answered `landed:refs/heads/pier/...` for a
# record standing where every reader walks past, and this guard read `unlanded=0 verdict=ok` over a
# complete unlanded feature. `parked` is reported beside the gate rather than gated on its own,
# since two readings that always fire together are one reading wearing two names.
#
# WHAT THE GATE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT REACH: the stash itself. A record reads landed whether or not
# its stash still stands, so the only way to turn this green is to put the record back in the
# channel. A meter a hand could satisfy by dropping evidence is a meter that teaches deletion.
#
# A RECORD IS NOT THE WORK (REDS %510), and it is the second question this gate owes an answer to.
# The session log serves as the proxy because every lap writes one, which is the one thing true of
# every lap. The proxy parts from its subject in a single direction -- a lap whose log lands while
# its code waits behind -- and `unlanded=0 verdict=ok` then stands over a box that still holds the
# files. So the scan reads every NON-record path by the same probe: `orphans` names what stands on
# no ref outside the box, `unread` names what a ref does carry and whose stashed EDIT a path probe
# leaves open, and `paths` is their sum.
#
# ORPHANS REPORT RATHER THAN GATE, because a COUNT stays local where a record travels. `unlanded`
# reads zero on every tree, since a record belongs in the channel everywhere; an orphan count is a
# per-checkout fact, so a ceiling measured on one ship would red another for parking more work. A
# file that landed under a different NAME reads as an orphan too, which lifts the live reading above
# the count of files anybody still wants. Measured `20260906.194500` on this field:
# `paths=48 orphans=9 unread=39`. SIX of the nine are REDS or ITINERARY fold shelves whose rows
# stand elsewhere -- four under a shelf a peer named differently, `%508` and `%509` unfolded on the
# living pin. THREE are work that stands on no ref: `sow_allow_reach_control.sh` (209 lines),
# `agent_jail_control.sh` and `mount_namespace_probe.sh` -- the pen and the probe that authorize
# `%446`'s skip, waiting in the box while the guard they were written for landed ahead of them.
# That is the reading the record gate leaves open, and it is why the second drawer earns a name at
# every open.
#
# AND NINETEEN ORPHANS ARE THREE KINDS (REDS %592). The count above was honest and unreadable: a
# hand who runs `list` gets one number's worth of paths wanting three different actions, with
# nothing telling them apart, so every ship read past all of them for a day and a half. Measured on
# this field `20260908.024426`, `orphans=19` sorted into `orphans_moved=3` -- this guard's own
# three files, stashed at their elder `tools/fixtures/f/` paths before the letter-room fold moved
# them to `s/` -- `orphans_shelf=10` fold shelves, whose rows come off the living pin so an
# unlanded shelf loses nothing, and `orphans_work=6`: a whole unlanded `standing_equipment_yield`
# guard family, `sow_allow_reach_control.sh`, `agent_jail_control.sh`, `mount_namespace_probe.sh`.
# Only the six are a lap, and thirteen-nineteenths noise is why nobody read any of it.
#
# THE THREE REPORT AND DO NOT GATE, like the count they partition -- plus a fourth reason of their
# own: `shelf` is an argument rather than a measurement, sound because a fold reads the pin and
# writes the shelf, and wrong for a lap that landed its pin edit and its shelf in two commits.
# Nothing turns on it, so a reader who distrusts the class reads the path printed beside it. What
# IS asserted here is that the partition holds and that the readings exist at all: a classifier
# that silently lost a kind would answer zero for it on every tree forever, which is the one number
# a healthy field and a blind instrument spell identically (%463).

say "stash-record: Language EN -- a session log parked at a round open is a record only once something carries it."
say "stash-record: Style Gauge, Meter -- every leg run on real repositories in a throwaway pen, never described."
say "stash-record: Lens TAME -- bound the walk (64 stashes, 512 records, 2048 paths), and name the refs rather than sweeping --all."

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the scan and its control both live.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the scan under test must stand before any reading of it is believed.
let present = run ["test" "-f" "tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh"]
assert present.ok else "tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh is missing -- the box has no reader"

# invariant: every planted case reads as planted, refusals and welcomes alike.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "stash-record: a planted case read wrong -- see the control's own lines"
assert control.out contains "fail=0" else "stash-record: the control closed with a failing leg"

# invariant: the reading on THIS tree, which is the one the fleet lives in.
let here = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh"]
assert here.ok else "stash-record: the scan refused on this tree"
say here.out
assert here.out contains "unlanded=0" else "stash-record: a session log stands in a round-open stash and nothing else carries it -- run `sh tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh list` and read it back"
assert here.out contains "parked=0" else "stash-record: a record is carried only by a pier/ park branch, which is the second drawer of the same box rather than the channel -- run `sh tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh list`"
assert here.out contains "verdict=ok" else "stash-record: the box holds a record the channel does not"

# invariant: the scan reads the park namespace at all. A reading that silently lost its exclusion
# would answer `parked=0` on every tree forever, which is the one number indistinguishable from a
# healthy field (REDS %463) -- so the presence of the exclusion is asserted rather than assumed.
let excludes = run ["grep" "-F" "-q" "^refs/heads/pier/|^refs/remotes/" "tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh"]
assert excludes.ok else "stash-record: the scan no longer excludes the pier/ park namespace, so a park would read as a landing again"

# invariant: the path walk is present at all. It is reported rather than gated, so a walk that
# silently vanished would answer `orphans=0` on every tree forever -- the one number a healthy
# field and a blind instrument spell identically (%463). Its presence is asserted rather than
# assumed, exactly as the park exclusion above is.
assert here.out contains "orphans=" else "stash-record: the scan no longer reads the paths beside the records, so the work in the box would read as nothing at all"
assert here.out contains "unread=" else "stash-record: the scan no longer names the paths it cannot judge, and an unprinted reach is claimed by implication"

# invariant: the three kinds are read at all. Each is asserted by name rather than the group, since
# a classifier that lost ONE kind would fold its members silently into another and the total would
# still balance -- the partition below cannot see that, and these three can.
assert here.out contains "orphans_moved=" else "stash-record: the scan no longer tells a moved orphan from a lost one, so this guard's own elder paths would read as parked work"
assert here.out contains "orphans_shelf=" else "stash-record: the scan no longer tells a fold shelf from a lap, and a shelf checked out is a rollback rather than a recovery"
assert here.out contains "orphans_work=" else "stash-record: the scan no longer names the orphans that are actually a lap, which is the only one of the three worth a hand"

# invariant: and every orphan is given exactly one kind. The scan sums the three against the count
# it partitions and says which it got; a partition stated in a header and never checked is a
# partition that drifts on the lap somebody adds a fourth kind.
assert here.out contains "orphan_kinds=partition" else "stash-record: the orphan kinds no longer sum to the orphan count, so a path is being reported twice or not at all -- run `sh tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh all`"

# invariant: the round open actually calls the reading, or the report exists and nobody hears it.
let wired = run ["grep" "-q" "stash_record_scan.sh" "tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh"]
assert wired.ok else "stash-record: the round open no longer reads the box it fills"

# invariant: and it reads BOTH drawers. The record line was wired at %464; the orphan line is what
# %510 added, and a reading nothing prints is a reading nobody acts on.
let wired_orphans = run ["grep" "-q" "orphans=" "tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh"]
assert wired_orphans.ok else "stash-record: the round open reads the records and not the work beside them"

say "stash-record: GREEN -- every record the dead-letter box holds is carried by the channel too, and a pier/ park is not the channel."
